WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.400
New this

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:00.834
morning, the

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.668
Russian capital

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.269
getting a firsthand sense of war

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.704
after an alleged drone attacks.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.339
You see a plume of smoke there

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.375
in the center of your screen rising.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.275
And you can actually see

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.377
in this next video,

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:11.845
you see a drone flying over the city.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:12.679
You'll see in just a moment.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:13.179
See this man?

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.814
They're pointing it out as he looks at it

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.483
out of his window.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.484
There is also video

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.852
that's been posted of what appears to be

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:21.221
a fragment of a downed drone.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.188
Russian state

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:22.822
media says two

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.257
people were injured in Moscow

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.625
and three residential buildings

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.360
were damaged in the attack.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.795
Russian military officials are blaming

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.063
Ukraine for the attack.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.098
Something Ukraine denies.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:32.732
We should note that

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.199
attack came

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.801
just hours after another aerial

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:35.835
assault on Kiev.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:36.803
Ukrainian officials

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.471
say one woman was killed.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.873
13 others were injured.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.275
There have been 17 attacks on Kiev so far

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.176
this month.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.911
Ahead of the planned counteroffensive.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.478
And officials

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:48.214
just released this body camera video

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.182
and to that of police

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.817
responding to one of the attacks.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:51.451
A real time

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.987
look at the daily reality of war

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.289
as officers help injured civilians.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.358
Joining us now from CNN,

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.993
former CNN Moscow bureau chief

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:00.593
Jill Dougherty.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.961
She's an adjunct professor

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.096
at Georgetown University.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:03.630
Good morning, Jill.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.864
I'm glad you could join us

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:05.865
last minute this morning

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.467
just to get your reaction

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.769
to this continued bombardment on Kiev

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.071
and then also what we saw

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.572
take place in Moscow.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.642
Yeah, I think

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:16.176
what happened in

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.311
Moscow is really significant.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:19.412
You know,

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.580
there have been attacks

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.781
by apparently

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.650
Ukrainians over the border

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.718
close to Ukraine.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.954
But this is Moscow. This is a big deal.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.622
Moscow is protected

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:33.093
by very serious air defenses.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.761
And they say

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:35.995
the Russian officials say

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.131
that these drones were shot down,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.632
but just in the air of fact.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.201
Remember, a month ago

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.335
we had that drone,

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.537
two drones that went over the Kremlin

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:45.705
and the Kremlin

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.173
in the beginning wasn't quite sure

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.241
how to deal with it.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.210
Kind of the same thing here.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.645
They haven't really been able to deal

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.179
with the,

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.415
I would say, in a propaganda way

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.816
with what's happening.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:58.852
And, you know, if you look at the drones,

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.019
the damage

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.489
militarily is not really great.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.891
But the propaganda value really

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.327
is to the dilemma by Putin

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.497
You know, you could say he has to admit

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.098
that the war is expanding

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.299
and that it's hitting

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.534
the Russian capital.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.569
That's very bad for him politically.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.704
On the other hand,

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.872
I think what you're going to see

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:19.506
is the Kremlin

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.740
trying to spin this,

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.676
that the war, you know, now we have like

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:24.477
this is

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:28.414
until this survival of Russia, etc.,

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:29.382
they will use it

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.518
to try to get the Russian people united.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.418
But I think

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.588
it's really a very disturbing thing for

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:38.124
Putin. It's a real problem for him.

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:39.993
So they'll try to spin that into

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:40.827
some other propaganda.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:41.594
I find it interesting.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.263
Our CNN military analyst, Colonel Cedric

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.497
Leighton, said this morning

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.465
very clearly

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.167
he says this is a warning

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.968
to the Russian people.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.170
How do you think the Russian people are

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:50.970
taking it today?

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:53.139
Well, I've been

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.040
on social media

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.942
and can start to figure out

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.010
what they're thinking.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.211
It's kind of hard to say,

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.613
but I think there's an element of shock.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:01.981
There's no question

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.850
that drones have actually now

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.319
not just kind of symbolically gone

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.587
over the Kremlin,

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.622
but now they're hitting neighborhoods.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.491
And I looked at a map

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.692
of where those winds hit.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.394
So they're in the city.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.628
And then outside

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.130
and they're in areas

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.698
kind of west of Moscow

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.867
where you have a lot of elite housing.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:23.169
The president lives out in that area.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.872
So this is this is really significant,

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:28.274
even if, again, the damage is minimal.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:31.110
But the psychological damage, I think, is

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.379
quite strong.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.583
Jill Dougherty, thank you very much.

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.318
CNN's Fred Pleitgen is in Kiev.

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.253
He's outside some buildings

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.588
that were damaged

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.289
where they were damaged overnight.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.291
Fred, you spoke to the city's mayor.

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:46.459
What is he saying today?

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:49.963
Father Kate?

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:50.897
Well, Vitali Klitschko,

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:51.764
the mayor of the city,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:52.832
was absolutely irate

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:53.833
about this drone attack.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:54.834
He called it terrorism

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.102
on the part of the Russians.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:56.936
But he also said that

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.404
actually the Ukrainian air defense

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.505
was pretty successful

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.840
and it was successful

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.041
thanks to a lot of the weapons

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.543
that Ukrainians are getting from

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.844
the US and its allies.

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:05.878
Let's listen in.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.282
If we doesn't have

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:10.683
our defense model on air

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.885
defense from our partners,

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.220
we have

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.656
a much worse situation in our hometown.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:19.525
More destroy the buildings and more

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:24.330
it will be more civilians killed

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:26.833
So one of the reasons, Kate,

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:27.400
why Vitali

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.134
Klitschko said

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:28.935
that I want to show you

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.003
that this building here

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.004
that I'm standing in front of,

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:32.071
this is the one of the ones

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.573
that sustained a lot of building

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.774
because it took a hit

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.042
from one of those shadow drones

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.377
that's supplied by the Iranians.

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:38.444
But the Russians are using.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.212
You can actually hear

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:39.545
and see

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.513
that a lot of clean

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.514
up is already going on.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:42.415
If we pan up,

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.182
you can see that

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.684
that drone crashed

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.452
right into the top floors

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.320
of this building.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.022
Now, one person was killed there.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.356
However, even that drone

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.157
that crashed into this

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:53.092
building was intercepted.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:53.893
It was intercepted

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.461
by Ukrainian air defenses.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.163
And they say that it was the fragments

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.531
of that drone, obviously,

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.766
including the warhead

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:01.034
that crashed into that building.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.135
But I can tell you,

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:02.735
it was certainly

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.771
a very difficult night here for the folks

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:05.605
in the capital city.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.906
We heard those

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:07.573
those drones

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:08.841
hovering overhead

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:09.642
for a substantial

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.243
part of the night,

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:12.512
several hours as Ukrainian air defenses

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.580
were trying to take them out.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.348
At the same time,

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:16.082
you do feel

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.550
that resilience here

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.885
in the Ukrainian capital

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.553
as now only hours later,

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.688
the cleanup is going on

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.089
and people are trying to go

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:24.390
about their daily lives.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.558
This, of course, comes

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.927
as Ukraine seems to be on the cusp

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.195
of that counteroffensive.

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:30.296
And Ukraine's president

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:30.997
now saying

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:32.398
the timing of that to set

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.801
the offensive has now been decided Kate.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:35.301
Yeah.

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:36.602
Not telling you exactly one,

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:37.570
but that it has been decided.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.771
And just to be clear, that's cleanup.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:39.238
That's people

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.707
throwing like debris

00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:42.575
off the off the rooftop behind you, Fred.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.546
Yeah, that's exactly what's going on.

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:48.047
There was substantial damage

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:49.649
to the top floor apartments there.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:50.216
And now they're sort

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:51.417
of clearing the debris,

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.352
throwing it down to then

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.152
be able to clean it up

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:53.953
as fast as possible.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.488
They are pretty quick at doing that now.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:56.389
Unfortunately,

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:57.357
they have a lot of practice

00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:58.491
after a lot of the strikes

00:05:58.491 --> 00:05:59.058
that have happened here

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.059
over the past year.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.361
That's a great that's a great point.

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:01.794
Unfortunately,

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.129
they've become very good at that cleanup

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:03.663
very quickly.

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:04.097
Thank you,

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:06.132
Fred Pleitgen on the scene for us John.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:06.366
All right.

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:07.700
With us now is retired

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.135
Brigadier General Peter, his work.

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:10.236
He is a global fellow

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:12.071
at the Wilson Center's Kennan Institute.

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:12.538
And served

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.874
as the US senior defense SSA

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.542
to the Russian Federation.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:17.343
General, look,

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.245
I want to start with the drone attacks

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:20.880
on Moscow up here,

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.482
which is the Ukrainian border,

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:24.217
about 300 miles, depending on

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:24.817
what direction

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:27.120
you go from inside Ukraine.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.554
I want to show people

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.423
the sights inside

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.358
Russia or in Russian control.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:33.426
Territory

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:34.594
that have been hit

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:36.062
over the last several weeks.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:36.429
You can see

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.797
most of the areas

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:39.532
have to do with the Russian occupation

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:40.800
directly of Ukraine, either

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.135
supply areas

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:44.837
or Russian held territory inside Ukraine.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:46.572
Moscow

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:49.575
stands alone as a much different target.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:50.743
Now, the Ukrainians deny

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.111
direct involvement

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:55.114
But what do the drone attacks in Moscow

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:56.549
do for the Ukrainians,

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:58.684
even if they didn't do it

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.221
Good morning, John.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:04.957
And to your viewers.

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:07.126
Yeah, it is highly significant.

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:09.495
What we have going on here

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:11.397
is that the Russians are being fed

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:14.667
a narrative about the justness of this

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:18.104
military, the special military operation.

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.373
And they're going to prevail.

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:23.409
Yet they are they just had the Kremlin,

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:26.312
however it happened, hit last month.

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:30.016
They've just had Moscow and the suburbs

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:32.318
hit now.

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:36.122
And the drones are coming from somewhere.

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:37.690
It's an extreme

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:38.591
range for

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:41.027
if you will, the Ukrainian organic drones

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:42.528
or the

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:44.530
the doctors from Turkey,

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.932
if they were far from the border.

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:47.333
But the bottom line

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:50.102
is that they can't hide the war

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.506
from if you well, call the Saudis now,

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:55.608
what I would call mainstream Russia,

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:56.776
the bill payers.

00:07:56.776 --> 00:07:57.977
Most of the war in Ukraine

00:07:57.977 --> 00:08:00.246
had been most troops from the provinces,

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.482
but now they're having to deal with it.

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:03.182
And the

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:05.318
and the military bloggers are out there.

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:07.687
Prigozhin has already lambasted

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.856
the military again

00:08:09.856 --> 00:08:11.991
just just a few hours ago

00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:13.593
for their ineffectiveness

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.828
in defending the motherland.

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:19.665
And so this is very disconcerting for

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:22.335
for Putin and the Kremlin

00:08:23.069 --> 00:08:24.837
in trying to keep it to

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:26.038
a stable narrative.

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:27.139
It's a big deal,

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:29.475
much bigger than the actual

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:31.677
sum of the strikes again.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:32.512
And this is some video

00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:34.213
of what the strike look like

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:35.581
inside Moscow.

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:38.351
That type of image is seen in Kiev

00:08:38.651 --> 00:08:41.120
almost every time, several times a day.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.321
This is some of the video

00:08:42.321 --> 00:08:43.189
on the attacks on Key,

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:44.223
which have been relentless,

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:44.957
frankly,

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:46.292
over the last several days,

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:48.160
day and night.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.929
Why are the Russians striking

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:51.631
now with such ferocity in

00:08:51.631 --> 00:08:52.598
the Ukrainian capital?

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:56.469
I think for several.

00:08:56.469 --> 00:08:57.370
First of all,

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:00.006
I was there with the delegation

00:09:00.006 --> 00:09:02.441
of the Renewed Democracy

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:05.011
Initiative, an NGO focused on

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:07.647
countering authoritarianism

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:09.015
worldwide domestically.

00:09:09.015 --> 00:09:10.449
Now, here,

00:09:10.816 --> 00:09:12.451
I think it's a bunch of reasons.

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:13.786
One, there's fury

00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:14.754
there's anger

00:09:14.754 --> 00:09:17.490
that it's been going on now for months,

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:19.659
but especially after Kremlin strike.

00:09:19.659 --> 00:09:21.394
There's a side of the Russians, John,

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:23.429
that I believe they want.

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:25.831
They want the Ukrainians to submit.

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:26.799
It's a word

00:09:26.799 --> 00:09:29.268
that's almost medieval submit,

00:09:29.468 --> 00:09:30.403
and they aren't.

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:32.271
And the more the Ukrainians fight back

00:09:32.271 --> 00:09:33.339
and the more the Ukrainians

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:34.874
create problems in the area,

00:09:34.874 --> 00:09:36.409
the harder it gets.

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:37.977
And they haven't figured it out.

00:09:37.977 --> 00:09:38.878
I also think

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:40.112
increasingly the Russians

00:09:40.112 --> 00:09:41.847
are now trying to

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:43.683
they're really nervous about the

00:09:43.683 --> 00:09:44.817
the all the talk

00:09:44.817 --> 00:09:46.052
about a counter-offensive

00:09:46.052 --> 00:09:47.787
in the preparations,

00:09:47.787 --> 00:09:50.556
the the shaping operations, everybody.

00:09:50.756 --> 00:09:52.692
And so that's going on.

00:09:52.692 --> 00:09:55.061
So they're lashing out in a way.

00:09:55.061 --> 00:09:57.363
And and the thing that's critical

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.498
is that these are not hitting

00:09:59.498 --> 00:10:01.400
effectively military targets.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.469
They're primarily hitting targets

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:04.804
where there are a lot of civilians

00:10:04.804 --> 00:10:05.671
and they're killing.

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:07.473
And if the Russians think

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:08.007
that's going

00:10:08.007 --> 00:10:08.774
to make

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:10.710
the Ukrainians submit,

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:11.677
from our view

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:13.613
in my group that I was with,

00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:14.347
we were there

00:10:14.347 --> 00:10:16.349
for the first big night of the missile

00:10:16.349 --> 00:10:19.285
strikes in Kiev on the 16th of May

00:10:19.485 --> 00:10:20.953
when the Patriots

00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:23.055
and other things were knocking down

00:10:23.055 --> 00:10:25.691
notch kings, all Russian cruise missiles.

00:10:25.891 --> 00:10:29.996
So it's on Ukrainians are implacable.

00:10:30.563 --> 00:10:32.732
The Russians are increasingly frustrated

00:10:32.732 --> 00:10:34.033
and they're increasingly worried.

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:34.800
And I think it goes

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.869
all the way back to the Kremlin.

00:10:36.869 --> 00:10:37.770
General Peter Zack,

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:38.871
thank you so much

00:10:38.871 --> 00:10:39.705
for helping us this morning.

00:10:39.705 --> 00:10:40.640
We'll talk to you again soon.

